{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.QBeta.DTChiralityBarInvolutionLink","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.QBeta.DTChiralityBarInvolutionLink","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:QOU.QBeta.ChiralityGradedCount","lean:module:Mathlib.Algebra.GroupWithZero.Basic"],"declarations":17,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.DTChiralityBarInvolutionLink.instDTBarInvolutionLinkSplit","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.DTChiralityBarInvolutionLink.instDTBarInvolutionLinkSplit","kind":"instance","line":152,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/DTChiralityBarInvolutionLink.lean#L152-L158","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.DTChiralityBarInvolutionLink.amphichiral_datum_consistent","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.DTChiralityBarInvolutionLink.amphichiral_datum_consistent","kind":"theorem","line":137,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/DTChiralityBarInvolutionLink.lean#L137-L144","doc":"**Conditional `4₁` consistency**: an amphichiral knot datum must carry an\nequal split — the literature `(3, 3)` satisfies this, so the link is consistent\nwith the `4₁` record. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.DTChiralityBarInvolutionLink.five_two_datum_forces_chiral","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.DTChiralityBarInvolutionLink.five_two_datum_forces_chiral","kind":"theorem","line":129,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/DTChiralityBarInvolutionLink.lean#L129-L135","doc":"**Conditional `5₂` chirality**: any knot datum whose DT reading is the\nliterature `(4, 3)` split is chiral under the link. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.DTChiralityBarInvolutionLink.jones_mirror_bar_inv","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.DTChiralityBarInvolutionLink.jones_mirror_bar_inv","kind":"theorem","line":115,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/DTChiralityBarInvolutionLink.lean#L115-L123","doc":"**Coherence (direction reversal)**: the bar law also runs backwards —\n`J_K(q) = J_{m(K)}(q⁻¹)`. Derived from the transformation law at the mirror\nknot plus involutivity (not a bare `symm` of the field): the mirror involution\nand `q ↦ q⁻¹` implement the *same* ℤ/2 action from either side. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.DTChiralityBarInvolutionLink.jones_bar_fixed_of_amphichiral","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.DTChiralityBarInvolutionLink.jones_bar_fixed_of_amphichiral","kind":"theorem","line":107,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/DTChiralityBarInvolutionLink.lean#L107-L113","doc":"**Amphichirality forces the invariant bar-even** (σ-fixed): the generic form\nof `FigureEightSelfDuality`'s 4₁ statement, derived from the link. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.DTChiralityBarInvolutionLink.chiral_dt_forces_chiral","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.DTChiralityBarInvolutionLink.chiral_dt_forces_chiral","kind":"theorem","line":99,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/DTChiralityBarInvolutionLink.lean#L99-L105","doc":"**The bar-odd DT part is a chirality obstruction**: a chiral split forces\nthe knot itself chiral (`5₂` from its `(4,3)` datum, conditionally). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.DTChiralityBarInvolutionLink.barOdd_dt_eq_zero_of_amphichiral","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.DTChiralityBarInvolutionLink.barOdd_dt_eq_zero_of_amphichiral","kind":"theorem","line":91,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/DTChiralityBarInvolutionLink.lean#L91-L97","doc":"**Amphichirality kills the bar-odd DT part.** A knot fixed by mirroring has\n`S⁺ = S⁻` — the `4₁` degeneracy, derived rather than observed. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.DTChiralityBarInvolutionLink.barOdd_dt_mirror","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.DTChiralityBarInvolutionLink.barOdd_dt_mirror","kind":"theorem","line":85,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/DTChiralityBarInvolutionLink.lean#L85-L89","doc":"The bar-odd part of the DT datum is mirror-negated — it is the `−1`\neigenvector, the chirality witness. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.DTChiralityBarInvolutionLink.barEven_dt_mirror","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.DTChiralityBarInvolutionLink.barEven_dt_mirror","kind":"theorem","line":79,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/DTChiralityBarInvolutionLink.lean#L79-L83","doc":"The bar-even part of the DT datum is mirror-invariant — it is the\nchirality-blind shadow (`7` for `5₂`). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.DTChiralityBarInvolutionLink.DTBarInvolutionLink.jones_mirror_bar","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.DTChiralityBarInvolutionLink.DTBarInvolutionLink.jones_mirror_bar","kind":"theorem","line":73,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/DTChiralityBarInvolutionLink.lean#L73-L73","doc":"**Hypothesis 2** (the Jones mirror rule): mirroring is the bar\ninvolution on the invariant. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.DTChiralityBarInvolutionLink.DTBarInvolutionLink.dt_mirror_swap","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.DTChiralityBarInvolutionLink.DTBarInvolutionLink.dt_mirror_swap","kind":"theorem","line":70,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/DTChiralityBarInvolutionLink.lean#L70-L70","doc":"**Hypothesis 1**: mirroring swaps the split. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.DTChiralityBarInvolutionLink.DTBarInvolutionLink.jones","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.DTChiralityBarInvolutionLink.DTBarInvolutionLink.jones","kind":"def","line":68,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/DTChiralityBarInvolutionLink.lean#L68-L68","doc":"The carrying `q`-invariant (Jones-type). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.DTChiralityBarInvolutionLink.DTBarInvolutionLink.dt","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.DTChiralityBarInvolutionLink.DTBarInvolutionLink.dt","kind":"def","line":66,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/DTChiralityBarInvolutionLink.lean#L66-L66","doc":"The chirality-split DT reading `(S⁺, S⁻)`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.DTChiralityBarInvolutionLink.DTBarInvolutionLink.mirrorK_involutive","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.DTChiralityBarInvolutionLink.DTBarInvolutionLink.mirrorK_involutive","kind":"theorem","line":64,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/DTChiralityBarInvolutionLink.lean#L64-L64","doc":"Mirroring is an involution. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.DTChiralityBarInvolutionLink.DTBarInvolutionLink.mirrorK","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.DTChiralityBarInvolutionLink.DTBarInvolutionLink.mirrorK","kind":"def","line":62,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/DTChiralityBarInvolutionLink.lean#L62-L62","doc":"Knot mirroring. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.DTChiralityBarInvolutionLink.DTBarInvolutionLink.mk","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.DTChiralityBarInvolutionLink.DTBarInvolutionLink.mk","kind":"ctor","line":60,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/DTChiralityBarInvolutionLink.lean#L60-L60","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.DTChiralityBarInvolutionLink.DTBarInvolutionLink","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.DTChiralityBarInvolutionLink.DTBarInvolutionLink","kind":"class","line":53,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/DTChiralityBarInvolutionLink.lean#L53-L73","doc":"**The D4 link, as an explicit conditional hypothesis class.** `K` is a type\nof knot data with a mirror involution, `dt` the chirality-split DT reading, and\n`jones` the carrying `q`-invariant. The two transformation fields assert that\nmirroring acts on the DT pair by the swap and on the invariant by the bar\ninvolution `q ↦ q⁻¹` — making the chirality split and bar parity the same ℤ/2\naction. Both are hypotheses (literature transformation laws), not corpus\ntheorems; see the module docstring. ","signatureChunk":0}]}